# Copy to the gitignored `.env` and fill in. Paths outside the repo are named *_ROOT variables;
# their values never appear in tracked files (check:local-paths).

# read-only reference site the core is extracted from
REFERENCE_SITE_ROOT=

# the site's private repo, which keeps the site's planning and docs moved out of the core
SITE_REPO_ROOT=

# Owner strings for check:identity, one per line. Locally prefer the gitignored `.identity-denylist`
# file; CI reads the IDENTITY_DENYLIST secret. A set but empty variable means "no list": the gate then
# checks only its patterns with a warning (fails in CI), and check:publication-tree fails, so leave it
# commented out when the file is used. The generic patterns miss repo paths and
# e-mails, so list: the reference repo name, every site domain, the owner's name and e-mail, and the
# account and bucket names. A line `!<context>` allows the entries only inside that context, e.g. the
# npm scope `!@<scope>/` or the repository URL `!github.com/<owner>/`; elsewhere they still fail.
# IDENTITY_DENYLIST=
